  "description" : "Per-pixel harmonic regression (annual + sub-annual Fourier terms) across a multi-date collection: y(t) = a0 + \u03a3_k [ a_k\u00b7sin(2\u03c0kt/365.25) + b_k\u00b7cos(2\u03c0kt/365.25) ] with t in real acquisition days since the collection reference epoch. Solved in closed form (weighted least squares) with optional IRLS outlier damping. Outputs one fitted band per acquisition date plus RMSE and R\u00b2; optionally the raw coefficients. Pixels with fewer than minObservations valid samples stay NoData.",
  "display_name" : "Temporal Harmonic Fit",
